A||||7||Refio||Bosch plugs did make a difference!
Z||000000||Refio||05-15-99||06:08 AM||||Managed to get to the 3 rear plugs with the 3-inch ext! Noticed they were a little more rusted than the front 3. Gee I wonder why? I used Bosch platnium plugs and now runs like a dream! MUCH MORE POWER!
Z||000001||Patrick||05-15-99||10:47 AM||||<br>Was it the <b>Bosch</b> plugs that were responsible for the increase in power?<p>Or was the increase in power simply due to the fact that the back plugs REALLY needed to be replaced with ANY new plug?<p>
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-15-99||03:27 PM||||I put the Bosch Platinum plugs in my Fiero back in 91 and i didn't really notice a differance. As far as the Split-Fire plugs go I put them in my 94 S-10 ZR2 and I did NOT notice any differance! I read somewhere on the net that Split-Fire is being sued for false advertising! I think any good plug will suffice. Of course that is my opinion I could be wrong.<br>
Z||000003||theogre||05-15-99||06:03 PM||||ignition changes of any kind generaly DO NOT increase horse power in any measuable way.<p>I use split fires, i've used halfe a hundred others too. The car seems (DIS motor) to like the S.F.'s as far as starting goes, but otherwise there is no change.<p>If you reed thru Moroso's web site,  <A HREF="http://www.moroso.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.moroso.com</A>  you'll find they flat tell you ignition changes don'e increase HP. They do solve other problems, like coil charge times at high rpm, spark loss in boosted (turbo/super) applications etc.
Z||000004||LEE498||05-15-99||10:28 PM||||I agree there is no spark plug made that <br>will give you horse power!! $25-30 is a <br>waste of money on plugs that will do the <br>same as factory plugs.That may just be <br>me but that's the way i see it. Spend <br>the extra money on synthetic oils! 
Z||000005||Pretender||05-15-99||11:58 PM||||Think about it, a hotter spark means better combustion in the cyl., that means more power, maybe not a whole lot but it DOES ADD POWER., why else would spark plugs be coming out w/ new 4 prong tech., all platnum or what ever there made of..because of it's hotter spark!...i have also heard from some people that chips and pullys don't add any power and that there friends even had the changes dyno-ed....again that was wrong and i proved it, not only by just "feeling" a difference but by running the car at the track every weekend. All in all, hotter burning plugs add some power granted not much but they do!.......happy racing :o)
Z||000006||EMF||05-16-99||11:35 AM||||yea, some of those nissan 4 cyliniders with 8 plugs seem to have good pickup, and more guts than they would if there was 4 spark plugs.<br>the more spark, the more violent the combustion, and we all know violence is cool ;&gt;
Z||000007||Hock||05-27-99||08:02 AM||||all of these aftermarket plugs do provide performance under the right conditions. first  you need the proper ignition system to make more power (such as MSD, Jacobs, Accel, ect). these aftermarket HiPo plugs work best with such combinations. as for spilt fires they are junk. i have never seen a good set of them yet. i wouldn't even put them in my lawn mower.
